    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "According to CBS news, Millennials are reporting higher levels of clinical anxiety, stress, and depression than any other generation at the same age.  To better understand the issue, I did a number of empathy interviews with my recently graduated friends, and I found that every single one of my 6 interviewed friends reported feeling unhappy, bored, lonely, and unfilled. When they were asked for more information about these negative emotions, they revealed that they felt them most strongly during nights and weekends -  during down time. They reported also that these feelings stem from ‘not having anything to do outside of work’ and not knowing many people in their city. \r\n\r\nI propose that these young adults need to learn how to be productive and fulfilled during down time. The solution - named me+ - therefore helps young adults find activities that they will enjoy during their down time - hobbies are curated for each user and a game plan is provided for entry into that hobby. In this way, young adults are given a structure for investing in their identity and finding purpose outside of work. \r\n\r\nDuring initial development, I tested various algorithms for curating personalized hobbies, and tried various strategies to get users to actually adopt new hobbies. To determine if the solution was successful, I observed how many users reported enjoying the use of me+, how many successfully start a hobby, and how many wanted to continue with this hobby. I also did interviews to determine if the user’s experience during her down times from work improved, and what that did for her overall sense of identity. \r\n\r\nI learnt from testing and interviews that some users really enjoyed using the solution and those users are not deterred very much by price/location but that the opposite is also true for those users who do not enjoy using the solution. I also found that the users who enjoyed the solution successfully started hobbies and intended to continue them, noting that they were surprised about these options they previously did not know of and empowered by the knowledge that they could now go out and start doing something new.",
